## Styling Rules

1. Use CSS custom properties from the design system — never hardcode colors/spacing/radius
2. Exception: status-specific colors (priority badges, success green, danger red) can be hardcoded
3. Use `<style scoped>` on every component
4. Mobile-first: base styles for mobile, `@media (min-width: 768px)` for desktop
5. Transitions: use `all 0.2s ease` as the standard transition
6. Icon sizing via `:deep(svg)` selector when inside scoped styles
7. Interactive elements: always include hover states and cursor changes
8. Disabled state: `opacity: 0.5; cursor: not-allowed`
9. Focus states: use `border-color: var(--color-primary)` with subtle box-shadow
10. Mobile first: base styles for mobile, `@media (min-width: 768px)` for desktop

---

## Accessibility (a11y)

1. Use semantic HTML elements (`<nav>`, `<main>`, `<aside>`, `<header>`, `<button>`, etc.)
2. All interactive elements must have `title` or `aria-label` attributes
3. Buttons must be `<button>`, not `<div>` with click handlers
4. Form inputs need associated labels or `aria-label`
5. Support `prefers-reduced-motion` via the `reducedMotion` user preference
6. Ensure proper color contrast (WCAG AA minimum)
7. Keyboard navigation: focusable elements in logical tab order

